From: iOSPlus10 display agent (dpu)
Subject: [PATCH] negroni panel: wake with the full on-command + PPS, long DSI packets from memory (0268)

Phone log 2026-10-26 13:24-13:30 (kernel local-20261026-074105, negronifb_sleep=1): every
wake logged "display on (sleep-out 133 ms, DCS ok, panel DBV 356)", but the panel stayed
black with a purple strip. 0258 woke the panel with 0x11 + 133 ms + 0x29 only and relied
on the S6E3HC3 keeping its registers in sleep-in. Android never does that: it sends the
whole DSI_CMD_SET_ON (dsi_panel_enable, dsi_panel.c:5708-5760) and then the DSC PPS
(dsi_panel_update_pps, dsi_display.c:9165-9170) on every display on.

NegroniBacklight.cpp:
- negroni_dsi_packet(): one packet with its own data type (0x05/0x15 short, 0x39/0x29/0x0a
  long). Up to 60 payload bytes from the TPG FIFO as before; longer packets from a command
  buffer in memory (dsi_ctrl.c:1701-1731 copy and pad, dsi_ctrl_hw_cmn.c:870-919
  kickoff_command: DMA_CTRL embedded, DMA_FIFO_CTRL watermarks off, DMA_CMD_OFFSET/LENGTH,
  SW trigger). Buffer: the last 16 KiB of the UEFI splash region (0xbaafc000; the 0234
  slots end there), read by the DSI DMA through the display SMMU context like the pipes'
  fetch. A memory DMA that times out turns the memory path off for the boot. 0269 ends the
  0234 display slots and surfaces at NEGRONI_DB_END (= the splash end - 16 KiB), so they never
  reach this buffer, whatever the page and row size.
- negroni_dsi_dcs_set_ex(): the set under a set lock (the 0259 VRR thread call and the wake
  never interleave inside an F0 5A 5A key), each packet with the type of the set (before:
  the type came from the length, "39 bd 21" went out as 0x15), flags to skip or go on after
  the long packets. negroni_dsi_dcs_set() and negroni_dsi_dcs_write() keep their API.
- Wake (negronifb_wake, default 2): auto-refresh paused (INTF_TEAR_AUTOREFRESH_CONFIG bit 31
  off, as _sde_encoder_autorefresh_disable_seq1), the 120 Hz FHD on-command from live.dts
  line 35658 (94 packets, LP: no on-command-state, dsi_panel.c:2678-2680), the 0x0A PPS
  (128 bytes, the UEFI XML PPS = the DT 9E PPS with version 0x12), auto-refresh back on,
  50 ms of TE/frame counters (re-arm once if TE but no frame), then the last DBV. The
  on-command ends in the 120 Hz state (60 00, BD[0x14]=00), so a 0259 VRR idle state before
  the sleep is undone by the panel itself; the 0259 exit set may come before or after it
  (set lock). =1: the on-command without the two long packets (FIFO only); =0: 0258.
  Log: "NEGRONI FB: display on (on-command 94 packets, PPS ok, TE on: N TE N frames tear 0x..
  in 50 ms, autorefresh 0x80000001 paused+resumed; sleep-out N ms, DCS ok, panel DBV N)".

NegroniFramebuffer.cpp: negroni_fb_autorefresh_pause/resume, negroni_fb_te_check (INTF_1
through fIntf, fMdss or an own page). Panic wake unchanged (0x11/0x29, no lock, no memory DMA).
Arrays: scripts/display/panel-dts-dump.py --on.

